Robot-side guard for 2026-FM-SystemCore (not committed there; apply by hand with `git apply`), against 827a91a
(check-ns-replay-merge). OrinSolver.solveOne() picks the alternate pose when its heading is closer to the gyro's.
PhotonVision's NAPA path published altCameraToTarget = (0,0,0) with poseAmbiguity 0 whenever AprilTag's orthogonal
iteration found one minimum (fixed in the fork, photonvision-106, and never the case in sc-vision), which places the
robot AT the tag; the alternate is then a wrong pose that can still win on heading. Ignore an alternate whose
translation is under 1 cm, or that is the same pose as the best.

--- a/src/main/java/frc/robot/subsystems/vision/OrinSolver.java
+++ b/src/main/java/frc/robot/subsystems/vision/OrinSolver.java
